+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Product review responses currently expose customer data, accept invalid or duplicate submissions, and leave product aggregates stale after moderation. This change makes review privacy, authorization, validation, conflict handling, and rating aggregates consistent for customers and merchants.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Restrict public review responses to review id, rating, description, date, and the reviewer's first name.
+- Validate customer review ratings as whole numbers from 1 through 5 and return HTTP 400 for invalid values.
+- Reject duplicate reviews for the same customer and product with HTTP 409, and reject customer-id impersonation with HTTP 403 without persisting data.
+- Support merchant review updates and deletion with product ownership checks and HTTP 404 for missing or mismatched reviews.
+- Recalculate product rating and rating count after review creation, update, and deletion, using one-decimal half-up rounding and zero values when no reviews remain.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `product-reviews`: Public, customer, and merchant product-review behavior and product rating aggregates.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected areas include the shop REST controllers and facades, review/product models and mappers, persistence services, and integration tests. The public review DTO is intentionally narrowed, and review endpoint status codes become part of the API contract.
